## Setup

Seed: 10,000 records × 30 typed fields for TWO tenants (tenant-load-a /
tenant-load-b) against the NCR template (35 fields, first 30 by sort order —
text/date/user/select/relation/checkbox/multiselect all exercised; relation
values point at a real clause-registry row). 20,000 `forms.records` +
600,000 `forms.record_values` total, inserted in 10 batch-transactions per
tenant. Counts verified per tenant: records=10000, values=300000 each.

FINDING (seed): the RDS master role BYPASSES RLS on Aurora — a values-INSERT
scoped only by `opened_by` matched the OTHER tenant's rows (caught by the
UNIQUE(record_id, field_id) violation, batch rolled back, reseeded with an
explicit tenant filter). Consequence recorded: master-credential SQL is NOT
RLS-scoped; every measurement below therefore runs through FormsFn (app_role),
and the cross-tenant probe is part of the gate.

## The gate, round by round

### Round 1 — BASELINE: FAIL (both surfaces)

| Surface | Result |
|---|---|
| `listFormRecords` | **Lambda timeout at 30.00s** (both tenants). The Task-3-accepted completion N+1 = 1 + 2×10,000 Data API round trips. Would also breach the AppSync 1MB response cap (10k rows unpaginated). |
| `getFormRecord` | wall p95 582ms / 486ms — borderline FAIL (4 sequential Data API round trips per read). |

### Rework 1 — N+1 removal + pagination (forms.ts, schema.graphql)

- `listFormRecords`: completion inputs ride the listing (LATERAL aggregate:
  `COUNT(*)` + `array_agg(field_key)` per row) + ONE template-fields query —
  2 round trips regardless of page size. SDL += optional `limit`/`offset`
  (server default 100, cap 500, newest first — documented, not silent).
- `getFormRecord` / `getFormRecordById` / `createFormRecord`: completion
  computed in code from the fields+values queries already made
  (`fetchTemplateFieldMeta` + `completionFrom`); `computeCompletion`'s 2
  extra round trips per read deleted.

### Round 2 — INTERMEDIATE: record read PASS, listing still FAIL

Lambda p95: get 301/296ms PASS; list 598/883ms FAIL (p50 436/522). EXPLAIN
ANALYZE as app_role showed why: a top-level LATERAL executes for ALL 10,000
candidate rows BEFORE the sort+LIMIT — aggregate loops=10000, 348.867ms
execution, and the scan used idx_forms_records_tenant then filtered
template_id and top-N-sorted 10k rows per call.

### Rework 2 — page-first subquery + migration 017 (the named index rework)

- Query rewritten: inner `ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT :limit OFFSET
  :offset` subquery FIRST, LATERAL aggregate over the returned page only
  (100 executions, ~3ms). Hermetic pin: `LIMIT :limit` must appear BEFORE
  `LEFT JOIN LATERAL` in the SQL.
- Migration `017_forms_register_index.sql`: `idx_forms_records_register
  (tenant_id, template_id, created_at DESC)` — the listing page is an
  ordered index walk under the RLS predicate; drops
  `idx_forms_records_template` (exact prefix, redundant). Applied via the
  ApiStack migrator (deploy 3), `_migrations` row
  `017_forms_register_index.sql` checksum 469330ae1775d059 verified; live
  `pg_indexes` shows register index present, template index gone.

### Round 3 — FINAL: **PASS** (2026-07-16 ~12:58Z, exit 0)

| Surface (Lambda-reported Duration, n per tenant) | tenant-load-a | tenant-load-b | target | verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| register listing p95 (n=30) | **235 ms** | **269 ms** | <500 ms | **PASS** |
| register listing p50 | 162 ms | 164 ms | — | |
| record read p95 (n=100) | **266 ms** | **272 ms** | <500 ms | **PASS** |
| record read p50 | 199 ms | 195 ms | — | |

Wall-clock (client, includes local network) also passes everywhere: list p95
336/310ms, get p95 406/417ms. Cross-tenant at scale: tenant-b reading a
tenant-a record id → RECORD_NOT_FOUND (RLS denial through the resolver).
Isolation of the page contents is RLS-enforced in the same SQL.

