## Carry-forwards (named, non-blocking)

1. Frontend register view calls `listFormRecords` without `limit` → shows the
   newest 100. Pagination controls (offset paging or infinite scroll) are a
   frontend follow-up; the SDL args are live and documented.
2. OFFSET pagination degrades linearly on deep pages (offset 9900 walks the
   index past 9900 entries). Fine at wave-1 scale; keyset pagination
   (`created_at < :cursor`) is the upgrade path if registers grow past ~100k
   records per template.
3. Master-role SQL bypasses RLS (BYPASSRLS on Aurora master) — recorded as a
   standing operational fact: never validate isolation with master
   credentials; the int-lane denial suite + resolver-path probes are the
   valid instruments.

